{"n": 727, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "727.webp", "text": "28 36023\n\n30 36024\n\n40 26030\n\n36-9\nREPLACING TIRES\n\nRefer to operating instructions supplied with pertinent tire mounting machine for correct mounting\nof tires. However, also make sure that the machine Is In perfect condition and that the wheel rim and\ntire are not damaged.\n\nGeneral Tire Removing / Mounting Instructions\n\nRemoving:\n\nBegin removal of a tire at the valve.\n\nAfter pressing the tire off of the rim flange, remove balance weights, press tire bead Into well and\ncoat thoroughly with tire mounting paste**. Clean wheel rim thoroughly and inspect rim for damage\nbefore mounting tire. The valve and valve insert must be replaced each time a tubeless tire is re-\nmoved and Installed.\n\nImportant!\n\nLoosen the tire on the inside and outside by applying the pressing-off horn on.the bead periphery at\nseveral points before pressing off the tire. Should it be difficult to press off the tire, pry the tire away\nfrom the rim flange as far as poss-ible with the pressing-off horn and then apply tire mounting paste\nbetween the tire and rim flange. Repeat this step around the complete periphery of the tire.\n\nThen press of the tire completely.\n\nGreater pressing-off force Is required for “TD tires” due to the bead toe seal. It is necessary to\nloosen tire on Inside and outside at several points around the bead periphery with the pressing-off\nhorn prior to pressing off.\n\nCaution!\n\nTD bead toe could jump out of Denloc groove suddenly and cause pressing-off horn to knock in!\n\nMounting;\n\nCoat tire bead with tire mounting paste**.\n\nMake sure tire Is mounted on correct side, especially in case of asymmetric tires. The “outside” of\nthese tires is marked.\n\nMount tire with as little as possible stress on the beads, since otherwise there would be danger of\ndamaging the tire or TD bead toe of TD tires.\n\nFirst of all let the tire bead ~ coming from the well — jump over the hump of the rim-shoulder.\ninflate the tire in steps while observing continuously.\n\nMaximum “jump-over pressure” = 3.3 bar (47 psi).\n\nHf the tire Is not seated on the rim correctly, increasing the inflation pressure will not improve the tire\nseating!\n\nInstead it will be necessary to press off both tire beads, apply another coat of tire mounting paste\nand to Inflate Ue tire again.\n\nincrease the Inflation pressure slowly until the tire “settles” only when the beads bear on the rim\nshoulders correctly.\n\nMaximum “settling pressure” = 4.0 bar (57 psi).\n\nRefer to Service Information of Group 36 for approved tires, tire sizes and wheel rims as well as\nspecial equipment.\n\nWe must point out that TD tires may be mounted only on TD rims!\n\nIncorrect mounting of TD tires on rims of other design (even TR!) could cause'tire damage, which in\nturn could lead to tire blowout while driving car.\n\nSuch tires may never be reused, not even on TD rims!\n\n** Source of Supply: HWB", "words": [["28", 0.2031, 0.502, 0.2138, 0.5106], ["36023", 0.2178, 0.5013, 0.2482, 0.5106], ["30", 0.1976, 0.7367, 0.2072, 0.7447], ["36024", 0.2107, 0.7374, 0.2401, 0.7454], ["40", 0.1986, 0.9582, 0.2057, 0.9708], ["26030", 0.2112, 0.9629, 0.2396, 0.9708], ["36-9", 0.4686, 0.0345, 0.5208, 0.0577], ["REPLACING", 0.2741, 0.0862, 0.3394, 0.0981], ["TIRES", 0.343, 0.0862, 0.3749, 0.0981], ["Refer", 0.2741, 0.1194, 0.3019, 0.13], ["to", 0.306, 0.12, 0.3161, 0.1306], ["operating", 0.3202, 0.1194, 0.3698, 0.1333], ["instructions", 0.3739, 0.12, 0.4367, 0.1313], ["supplied", 0.4407, 0.1207, 0.4853, 0.134], ["with", 0.4894, 0.1207, 0.5111, 0.1313], ["pertinent", 0.5157, 0.1207, 0.5623, 0.134], ["tire", 0.5664, 0.12, 0.5836, 0.1313], ["mounting", 0.5876, 0.12, 0.6373, 0.134], ["machine", 0.6418, 0.12, 0.6864, 0.1313], ["for", 0.69, 0.12, 0.7052, 0.1313], ["correct", 0.7082, 0.1207, 0.7462, 0.1313], ["mounting", 0.7508, 0.12, 0.8014, 0.134], ["of", 0.2741, 0.1353, 0.2842, 0.1472], ["tires.", 0.2877, 0.1359, 0.31